  "title": "A Grassmann proof of the Catalan divisor in the Teufl\u2013Wagner forest transfer determinant",
  "description": "<p>Credited, self-contained proof exposition of the all-n integral Catalan divisor in the full Bell-partition Teufl\u2013Wagner forest transfer determinant. Every input block uses one fixed arbitrary unweighted tree, and each admissible interlayer edge subset is counted once. The paired Grassmann forest algebra and Catalan quotient are established prior work; the exposition computes the induced determinant using ordered degree-triangular Gaussian factors and a constant rational kernel.</p><p>Alper Ferudun, Theorem 1.2, version 1.0, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23298482 (https://eulersolve.org/papers/owr-16164-020/), states the exact same all-n integral divisor with the same normalization. PR 1037 was created 2026-10-09T22:16:52Z (head commit 22:16:22Z); the matching DOI was registered 2026-10-11T13:01:38Z. Historical public visibility, independently evidenced discovery, intellectual priority and worldwide priority are unknown; no copying claim is made. The source review checked the matching core proof, but did not reproduce or validate its additional computer-assisted exactness claims.</p><p>Credits: Caracciolo\u2013Jacobsen\u2013Saleur\u2013Sokal\u2013Sportiello for the forest representation, Caracciolo\u2013Sokal\u2013Sportiello for forest/exponential/elimination identities, Sportiello Chapter 10 for the completed Catalan basis treatment, Kenyon\u2013Wilson for the equivalent quotient/projection and tree pairing, and Di Francesco\u2013Golinelli\u2013Guitter for associated meander nonsingularity (not a premise of this proof). The official thesis catalogue year is 2010; its cover academic years are not a publication date.</p><p>Version 1.0, dated 13 October 2026, by Alec Kriebel (ORCID 0009-0001-9320-500X), independent researcher. Extensive AI assistance in solving, verification, source comparison and writing; unrefereed AI audits, with no human refereeing, journal acceptance or formal certification. The theorem asserts a divisor only: no exact multiplicity, quotient irreducibility, complete factorization, first-solution, new-method, new-basis or current-open-status claim. Li\u2013Yan full-body overlap remains unknown; CSS 2017 and citation-chain/version comparisons remain partial. Authored text and code: CC BY 4.0. Frozen originals and fresh finite check evidence are distinguished. The supportkit records dated preparation checks and stage-specific AI reviews, each identified by scope and frozen inputs in REVIEW_HISTORY.json and EVIDENCE_INDEX.json. Those records are not human refereeing, journal acceptance, formal certification or submission/publication records.</p>",
